### The warning before sending a private key or seed phrase. **text** is bold.

secret-key-title = This is a private key
secret-seed-title = This is a seed phrase
secret-wallet-title = This is a wallet key
secret-key-text = Your message contains an **nsec**: the private key to a Nostr account. Whoever has it can read every private message, post as that account and take it over, for good. Once sent, it can't be taken back.
secret-seed-text = Your message looks like a **seed phrase**. Whoever has it can take everything in that wallet, instantly and for good.
secret-wallet-text = Your message looks like a **wallet private key**. Whoever has it can take everything in that wallet, instantly and for good.
# $place is the community's name.
secret-community = This is a community. Everyone in **{ $place }** would see it, and so would anyone who joins later.
# $place is who the chat is with.
secret-key-scam = No one ever needs your private key: not Vector, not support, not a friend. If **{ $place }** asked you for it, it's almost certainly a scam.
# $place is who the chat is with.
secret-wallet-scam = Scammers pose as support staff, giveaways and friends to ask for these. If **{ $place }** asked, stop and check who they really are.
secret-timer-offer = If you're sure, turn on a **Self-Destruct Timer** first, so it doesn't stay on devices and relays forever.
secret-timer-on = This chat's Self-Destruct Timer is on, so it won't stay on devices and relays.
secret-keep = Don't Send
secret-set-timer = Set a Self-Destruct Timer
secret-send = Send Anyway
# $seconds counts down until the button works.
secret-send-wait = Send Anyway ({ $seconds })
# Stands in for a channel with no name.
secret-this-community = this community
secret-pick-timer = Pick a timer, then send it again
